title: $:/plugins/lasjoh-toho/pinboard/readme

The ''Pinboard'' engine turns a [[TW5-Graph|$:/plugins/flibbles/graph]] graph into an infinite canvas: nodes become cards that show the fields you choose, you can draw and add shapes around them, and a path through the board plays back as a zooming, fullscreen presentation.

!! Getting started

Pick the template ''Pinboard (infinite canvas & presentation)'' in a graph's settings, or write the graph yourself:

```
<$graph $engine="Pinboard" store="My Board">
  <$list filter="[tag[Idea]]">
    <$node.default />
  </$list>
</$graph>
```

The `store` property names the tiddler that keeps the board's drawings, card sizes, chosen fields and presentation path (in its `pinboard` field). Without it, drawings only last until the board is re-rendered.

!! Menus

* ''Drawing dock'' (left): pen, highlighter, eraser, shapes, text, sticky note, new tiddler card, colors, stroke width, fill, undo/redo. Click the active tool again to go back to selecting.
* ''Navigation'' (bottom right): select, pan, the ''Lupe'' (zoom slider, show everything, show the selection, 100%, hide images), ''background'' (color, pattern: none/dots/grid/lines, picture from a tiddler or URL) and ''fullscreen''.
* ''Presentation'' (top right): ▶ present, frame tool, presentation path, layers.

!! Cards

* Drag a card to move it, drag its corner to resize it. Click an image to open it in a lightbox (fit or 1:1, scroll and drag to look around, Ctrl+wheel zooms).
* Hover a card for its tools: ''view'' (reader that is as tall as the tiddler, up to the whole screen; Edit/Close and "open in story river" appear on hover), ''fields'', ''link'' (then click the card to link to), ''add to path'', ''appear/disappear'', ''remove''.
* ''Fields'' chooses which fields this card shows and in which order. `title` toggles the card's heading; `text` renders the tiddler's body; `tags`, `created`/`modified`, `icon` get special treatment; any other field is shown as name and rendered value.
* ''Long tiddlers'': with `text` chosen, pick how much text the card shows on the board (whole text, up to the first `<br>` or blank line, the first image, or first image + text up to the first break) and, separately, in the presentation. A "more…" link opens the whole tiddler. Graph defaults: `textMode`, `presentTextMode`.
* Double-click a card to view it (unless the graph gives nodes their own `actions`). Drag the dot on a card's right edge to another card to connect them.
* Adding a tiddler (double-click on the board, or the card tool): type a title; if it does not exist yet, ''Create'' makes it.

!! Drawing

|Key |Tool |
|V |Select and move |
|H / Space |Pan |
|P |Pen |
|M |Highlighter |
|E |Eraser |
|R / O |Rectangle / ellipse (Shift: square / circle) |
|L / A |Line / arrow (Shift: 45° steps) |
|T |Text |
|N |Sticky note |
|F |Presentation frame |
|C |Add a tiddler card |

Selected shapes can be recolored, resized, rotated, moved with the arrow keys, sent behind or above the cards and deleted; Ctrl+D duplicates. A sticky note can be ''turned into a tiddler'' (first line = title, the rest = text, note color = tiddler color); it takes the note's place on the board. Double-click a shape to edit its text. Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Shift+Z undo and redo. Mouse wheel or pinch zooms, `0` fits everything.

''Layers'' (presentation menu) lists every drawing, shape, note and frame from top to bottom, with the cards in between. Drag a row's grip to restack it, past the cards to move it behind or in front of them; the eye hides it from board and presentation.

!! Presenting

Frames join the presentation path automatically. Cards, shapes and the current view can be added from their tools (target icon) or the path panel (list icon, top right), where stops are reordered by dragging their grip. ▶ starts the presentation: fullscreen, camera flights between stops.

* ''Tilted stops'': rotate a frame (or any box shape) with the round handle above it (Shift: 15° steps). The camera turns with it on arrival.
* ''Appear / disappear'': the eye icon on a shape or card picks the stop at which it appears and the stop at which it disappears.
* ''Reveals'': shapes lying on top of a card or shape vanish while the presentation shows what they cover, so a sticky note can hide an answer until its stop.
* ''Progress stack'': hover the counter at the bottom to see every stop as a bar (the last on top). Hover a bar for a live preview, click to jump.
* ''Pen'': the pen at the bottom left (or `P`) writes temporary notes on top of the presentation: pen, highlighter, text, eraser, colors, size, clear. Notes zoom with the board and are not saved.
* Cards set to show more text in the presentation grow to their fuller version when the presentation stops at them.
* Keys: arrows/Space/Enter, Home/End, `O` overview, `F` fullscreen on/off (also a button in the bar), `P` pen, Esc to leave. Clicks at the left/right screen edges step back and forth; drag and wheel explore freely.
* ''Export as HTML'' (path panel) downloads a single self-contained file that plays the presentation in any browser, without TiddlyWiki. It uses the very same player.

Messages for buttons inside the graph: `graph-pinboard-present` (optional `step`), `graph-pinboard-fit`, `graph-pinboard-open` (`tiddler`), `graph-center-node` (`tiddler`), `graph-move-view` (`x`, `y`, `scale`, `scaleBy`).
